aup-ssh

ssh into my AUP Learning Cloud workspace. the platform only gives you
jupyterlab / code-server in the browser, which gets painful for long llvm
builds and scripted test runs.

server.py runs inside the workspace as my user, asyncssh on localhost only,
key auth. proxy.py is the ProxyCommand on my laptop, it pipes the ssh stream
through the existing jupyter/code-server proxy using my logged in session.
on notebook images there's no port proxy so it goes through a jupyter
terminal instead (deleted when the connection closes, mostly).

doesn't start or stop compute, no sudo, nothing listening publicly.

start the server once from a browser terminal:
  nohup python3 ~/.local/share/aup-ssh/server.py > ~/.local/share/aup-ssh/server.log 2>&1 < /dev/null &

then:
  bin/aup-ssh 'hostname'

scripts/reap-aup-terminals.py cleans up terminals left behind by dropped
connections.

cookies.json and the keys sit in the same dir, gitignored.

tests: python -m unittest discover -p 'test_*.py'
